  "body": "## Full audit — stage 1: concurrency / real-action integrity\n\nThis stage fixes two correctness hazards found during the renewed production audit:\n\n1. A temporary cross-bot FIRST_OFFER claim could mark a competing per-bot listing terminal and then fail to reopen it if the competitor held a row lock during `SKIP LOCKED` cleanup.\n2. A stopped bot could be deleted while a real-action guard or unresolved marketplace claim still existed, destroying reconciliation evidence and leaving an orphaned global claim.\n\n### Changes\n- distinguish PRE-SUBMIT marketplace reservations from CONFIRMED durable claims (`V35`)\n- temporary claim conflicts leave competing listings `DISCOVERED`\n- only confirmed claims create `SKIPPED_ALREADY_NEGOTIATED`\n- pre-submit release is now a single ownership-checked delete; no reopen/`SKIP LOCKED` race\n- confirmed/stale FIRST_OFFER guard reconciliation marks the marketplace claim durable before guard cleanup\n- bot deletion is blocked by active real-action guards or unconfirmed marketplace claims\n- unit coverage for temporary vs confirmed claims and safe bot deletion\n- PostgreSQL CI smoke coverage for V33/V34/V35 and the new claim lifecycle\n\nDo not merge unless Backend, Playwright and Frontend CI are all green.",
